   "#The water cycle",
   "",
   "Water moves endlessly between the oceans, the air and the land.",
   "",
   "1. Evaporation: the Sun’s heat turns the water of oceans and lakes into water vapour, which rises into the air.",
   "",
   "2. Condensation: up high, the air is cold. The vapour cools down and forms tiny droplets: these are clouds.",
   "",
   "3. Precipitation: the droplets grow and fall back as rain, snow or hail.",
   "",
   "4. Run-off and infiltration: some water flows into rivers, then the sea; the rest soaks into the ground.",
   "",
   "Remember: water changes state (liquid, gas, solid), but the amount on Earth stays almost the same."
